$DIR/test.p:8:25: invalid argument: field f is embedded via a pointer in S
    This error occurs when unsafe.Offsetof is called with a method selector,
    rather than a field selector, or when the field is embedded via a pointer.
    "If f is an embedded field, it must be reachable without pointer
    indirections through fields of the struct. "
    (see "Package unsafe" in the Plutonium spec, section 20.1)
    (run "pluto explain E0099" for a longer explanation)
